//! The `border` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property sets an element's border. It sets the values of `border-width`, `border-style`, and
//! `border-color`.
//!
//! Initial: border-width: border-top-width,border-right-width,border-bottom-width,border-left-width;
//! border-style: border-top-style,border-right-style,border-bottom-style,border-left-style;
//! border-color: border-top-color,border-right-color,border-bottom-color,border-left-color.
//! Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - dashed: Displays a series of short square-ended dashes or line segments. The exact size and
//! length of the segments are not defined by the specification and are implementation-specific. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - dotted: Displays a series of round dots. The radius of the dots is half the computed value of
//! the line's width. The spacing of the dots is not defined by the specification and is
//! implementation-specific. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - double: Displays two straight lines with some space between them. The length of the lines adds
//! up to the pixel size defined by the line's width. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - groove: Displays a border with a carved appearance. This value is the opposite of `ridge`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - hidden: Displays no line. The [used
//! value](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Property_value_processing#used_value)
//! of the line width is `0` even if a width value is specified. In the case of table cell and border
//! collapsing, the `hidden` value has the _highest_ priority. If any other conflicting border is
//! set, it won't be displayed. The `hidden` value is similar to `none`, but `hidden` is not a valid
//! value for outline styles. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - inset: Displays a border that makes the element appear embedded. This value is the opposite of
//! `outset`. When applied to a table cell border and `border-collapse` is set to `collapsed`, this
//! value behaves like `groove`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - medium: Same as `3px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-width
//! - none: Displays no line. The [used
//! value](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Property_value_processing#used_value)
//! of the line width is `0` even if a width value is specified. In the case of table cell and border
//! collapsing, the `none` value has the _lowest_ priority. If any other conflicting border is set,
//! it will be displayed. The `none` value is similar to `hidden`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - outset: Displays a border that makes the element appear embossed. This value is the opposite of
//! `inset`. When applied to a table cell with `border-collapse` set to `collapsed`, this value
//! behaves like `ridge`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - ridge: Displays a border with an extruded appearance. This value is the opposite of `groove`.
//! See https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - solid: Displays a single, straight solid line. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-style
//! - thick: Same as `5px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-width
//! - thin: Same as `1px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-width
//!
//! Grammar: <line-width> || <line-style> || <color>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#propdef-border
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/border
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
